#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=9 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793974124784'; [Fri Nov 06 15:08:44 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!ITS haplotypes of the moss Syntrichia: 16 haplotypes of 951 sites with the number of samples of each as traits, from
the 116-sequence alignment ALIGNMENT_ITS_Haplotype_Network_116_SEQ of Saluga et al. (2022), Journal of Biogeography
49:1991-2004, Dryad DOI 10.5061/dryad.h18931zp3 (CC0). Figure 1 of the RazorNet paper: RazorHaploNet with the Shave filter.]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 16 taxa and 16 DNA sequences of length 951.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 30 nodes and 38 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 26 nodes and 28 edges.

References:
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

